  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Surgical and Medical Instrument Manufacturing (NAICS 339112) obligated $58.5M in FY2027 to date. The market recorded 328 awards with an average award size of $178K, and obligations fell 94.7% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations were $1.1B in FY22, $1.5B in FY23, $2B in FY24, $1.6B in FY25, $1.1B in FY26, and $58.5M in FY27 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs accounted for $58.4M of FY2027 to date buying. OLYMPUS AMERICA INC received $18.3M in FY2027 to date, and nine other vendors received amounts ranging from $6.9M to $1.1M. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial, reflecting fiscal year to date activity rather than full-year totals.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why did obligations fall so much year over year?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 94.7% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations were $2B in FY24 and then declined to $1.6B in FY25 and $1.1B in FY26, arriving at $58.5M in FY27 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs accounted for $58.4M of the FY2027 to date total."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the main buyers and suppliers in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the main buyer with $58.4M in obligations. The Department of Justice obligated $146K and the Environmental Protection Agency obligated $35.6K, while the Department of the Interior obligated $0. OLYMPUS AMERICA INC is the largest supplier with $18.3M, followed by SCRIPTPRO USA INC with $6.9M and HILL-ROM, INC. with $5.4M."
      }
    ]
  },
